  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SHO Middle East Response - Gaza 2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On the 7th of October, Gaza witnessed a sudden escalation of violence that has led to a devastating humanitarian crisis. 40,791 casualties, with 68% being women and children, alongside more that 100k injuries. Over 1,550 Palestinians, of whom 870 are children, are missing presumed trapped or dead under the rubble1. The violence has resulted in 1,487 male fatalities, leading to a surge in widows and nearly 900 new households led by women. Additionally, 3,103 children have lost their fathers, and this toll continues to rise in the absence of a ceasefire. UNFPA estimates 540,000 women of reproductive age in Gaza, with 50,000 pregnant and 5,522 expected to deliver in the next month 2. Since October 11th, Gaza has been in a full electricity blackout due to Israel&apos;s halt of electricity and fuel supply, forcing reliance on limited backup generators due to fuel scarcity. Approximately 1.4 million internally displaced people are estimated in Gaza, with nearly 580,000 sheltering in 150 emergency shelters, where overcrowding is a growing concern. Gaza lacks water, power, and fuel supplies, trapping 2.3 million people. The Israeli government advised nearly half the population to evacuate the north of the enclave, worsening the dire situation.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SUMMARY: This project is funded by the Dutch National Appeal, popularly known as Giro555 but run by the Stichting Samenwerkende Hulp Organisaties (Foundation Collaborating Aid Organisations), referred to as the SHO, who thus acts as the donor for this project. The SHO is itself made up of 11 of the country&#x2019;s largest humanitarian organizations, with Plan receiving approximately 5-8% of the proceeds. The general objective of this project is to contribute to humanitarian assistance to displaced families across the Middle and South of the Gaza Strip by providing them essential life-saving assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
